<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  automation-shortcut.plist

  Shortcut body designed to be triggered by a Personal Automation.
  Automation trigger is NOT part of the .shortcut file — the user
  creates the trigger binding in the Shortcuts app after import.
  This template is the action sequence to bind to that trigger.

  Demonstrates: silent operation (no UI actions), Set Focus,
  conditional on battery level, Show Notification for feedback.

  Suggested trigger: Time of Day 22:30.
  After importing this shortcut, create a personal automation:
    1. Open Shortcuts → Automation tab.
    2. + → Create Personal Automation → Time of Day → 22:30.
    3. Add Action → Run Shortcut → select this shortcut.
    4. Toggle "Ask Before Running" off.

  Customize:
  - WFBrightness: the night-mode brightness level.
  - WFNotificationActionTitle / Body: the feedback text.

  Sign and import:
    mv automation-shortcut.plist automation.shortcut
    shortcuts sign -i automation.shortcut -o automation.signed.shortcut -m anyone
    open -a Shortcuts automation.signed.shortcut
-->
